# Lighting

This layer is look only. Do not touch torques, colliders, or
`BalanceController`.

## Why URP

The project was on Built-in: `Sprites/Default` does not accept light.
In Unity 6, real 2D light is the **URP 2D Renderer** + `Light2D`
(not a 3D Light). Documentation 6000.5: Global / Spot(Point) / Freeform /
Sprite.

Pipeline: `Assets/Settings/URP-2D.asset` + `Renderer2D.asset`.
Created by `LightingPipelineSetup` when the editor opens.

## Light layers

| Layer | Type | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| Moon | `Light2D.Global`, Multiply, intensity 0.22, cold blue | night base. One Global per blend style |
| Torch | `Light2D.Point` 360°, Additive, intensity ~0.028, outer ~2.2 m | very dim local key. Perlin flicker in `Update` |
| Sky | Unlit, dark color | the sky is not a wall; the torch does not paint it |
| Body, dirt, slabs | `Sprite-Lit-Default` | accept Global and Point |
| Flame | Unlit, bright orange | the source lights itself |

Bloom (URP Volume, intensity 0.01, threshold 1.4) — almost off. HDR is on.
Normal maps are **off**: a full pre-pass on every batch does not pay off
on a ragdoll.
Do not attach `ShadowCaster2D` shadows yet: a long ground would make a
false wall.

Light Render Texture scale 0.5. Depth/stencil is off: there are no 2D
shadows. Max light RT is 4 (moon + torch), shadow RT is 0.

## Frame budget (college 28.08)

Do not cut physics or 200 Hz. The next measurement is the Profiler on
`World` (physics / scripts / Render2D), not a Hz sweep.

Look already taken out of the budget:
- torch volumetric is off
- Quality Ultra without 3D shadows, pixel lights, anisotropic, reflection
  probes; do not touch `vSyncCount` = 1 — otherwise FPS is about
  desync, not the frame
- URP-2D: 3D Main/Additional Light and the shadow atlas are off
  (light is Light2D only)
- Renderer2D without depth/stencil, light RT ≤ 4, shadow RT = 0
- Keep Interpolate on segments (smoothness at 60 Hz while physics is 200 Hz)
- the `-nographics` stand does not bake capsules and does not place
  joint markers

Do not do: MSAA, ShadowCaster2D on the ground, a second Point Light with
volume.

## Torch

`SceneLighting.Enabled` is **false** for now: no moon, no torch, no Bloom.
Sprites go Unlit so the frame is not black. Set `true` to restore night.

`Torch.Spawn` from `GameProcess` (Play Mode, not headless). No Rigidbody2D.
Stands at y = −2, 1.25 m ahead of the human.
Volumetric is off for the frame budget (`volumetricEnabled = false`,
`volumeIntensity = 0`); do not turn it on without a separate task.

## Do not

- 3D Light / Standard shader on sprites
- `HingeJoint2D.useMotor` and any light in `FixedUpdate`
- SIMBICON
- Attach Light2D to every body segment
- Enable volumetric on Light2D without a separate frame-budget task
